cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "vic-rent-ml: Fair temporal model selection for Victorian rental medians"
message: If you use this software or the accompanying study, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Valani
    given-names: Kelvin
    email: kelvin.valani@gmail.com
repository-code: https://github.com/kelvinvalani/vic-rent-ml
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-18"
abstract: >
  An open-source Python package and research write-up for forecasting Victorian
  suburb-group moving-annual median weekly rents. Candidates are compared with
  recursive temporal validation; the measured winner is Huber regression on
  quarterly rent changes with postcode features.
keywords:
  - rental forecasting
  - time-series cross-validation
  - Huber regression
  - Victoria Australia
